# Architecture

The application follows a modular frontend architecture.

Main structure:

src/
├── app/
├── components/
├── modules/
├── hooks/
├── theme/
├── types/
├── constants/
├── utils/
└── services/

Feature-specific functionality belongs inside:

modules/<feature>/

Recommended structure:

modules/<feature>/
├── components/
├── hooks/
├── models/
├── pages/
├── services/
└── utils/

Rules:

- Pages represent screens.
- Components represent UI.
- Hooks represent reusable behavior and state logic.
- Models represent domain types.
- Services represent feature operations.
- Utils contain pure functions.
- Shared functionality belongs outside feature modules only when genuinely reusable.
- Do not place business logic in pages.
- Do not place feature-specific code inside global components.
- Do not couple modules unnecessarily.